values ('a7b8c9d0-1e2f-4a15-8b45-5c6d7e8f9a75', 'history-of-ancient-philosophy', 'History of Ancient Philosophy', 'History of Ancient Philosophy introduces students to major Greek and Roman philosophical texts, arguments, schools, and methods from early natural philosophy through late antique reception. Students learn to read primary texts closely, reconstruct arguments, interpret fragments and testimonia, compare translations, understand historical context, and evaluate enduring questions about nature, knowledge, virtue, soul, politics, science, and the good life.');

